title: "On Intelligence and Its Specifications"
message: "If you reference this book in academic or critical work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alexander
    family-names: Towell
    email: lex@metafunctor.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6443-9897"
    affiliation: "Southern Illinois University Edwardsville"
abstract: >-
  A lay-readable book on the mathematics of optimal intelligence and what it
  implies about modern AI. It develops the clean theory of optimal prediction
  and decision (Bayesian inference, Solomonoff induction, and expected-utility
  maximization, synthesized as AIXI), then turns to the bounded systems that
  approximate it (large language models), and argues that the gap between the
  theory and the practice is where the specification problem, and AI safety,
  live. Seventeen chapters across four parts, written for the determined lay
  reader, with diagrams carrying much of the conceptual weight.
keywords:
